diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 30dacc3..905fd16 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -17,3 +17,27 @@ To install only for the current user, copy the files to "~/.themes".
 
 To set the theme in Plasma 5, install kde-gtk-config and use System Settings > Application Style > GNOME Application Style.
 Also make sure to disable "apply colors to non-Qt applications" in System Settings > Colors > Options.
+
+## Window background transparency
+
+Installed as the `Breeze-Transparent` and `Breeze-Transparent-Dark` GTK themes, next to stock Breeze.
+Window, headerbar and dialog backgrounds are translucent. The default opacity is set at build time:
+
+```sh
+cmake -DBREEZE_GTK_WINDOW_OPACITY=85 ..    # percent, 100 = opaque
+# or: build_theme.sh -o 85 ...
+```
+
+It can be changed per user without rebuilding with `breeze-transparent-gtk-opacity 70` (percent;
+`show` and `reset` are also available), then restarting GTK applications. This redefines the
+translucent colors in `~/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css` and `~/.config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css`, as follows:
+
+```css
+@define-color theme_bg_color_translucent_breeze alpha(@theme_bg_color_breeze, 0.7);
+@define-color theme_unfocused_bg_color_translucent_breeze alpha(@theme_unfocused_bg_color_breeze, 0.7);
+@define-color theme_titlebar_background_translucent_breeze alpha(@theme_titlebar_background_breeze, 0.7);
+@define-color theme_titlebar_background_backdrop_translucent_breeze alpha(@theme_titlebar_background_backdrop_breeze, 0.7);
+```
+
+Note: GTK themes cannot request background blur. On X11, GTK 3 windows without client-side
+decorations have no alpha channel and will look darkened instead; Wayland is recommended.
